{"id":"zpool-detach.8","n":"zpool-detach","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"zfsutils-linux","ver":"2.1.5-1ubuntu6~22.04.7","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/z/zfs-linux/zfsutils-linux_2.1.5-1ubuntu6~22.04.7_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/zpool-detach.8.gz","sha256":"5fbb7ea81e8cf04fef9a588e2146bfb25566ffc014aa15fc23fd4cc1a87d211d","date":"August 9, 2019","origin":"OpenZFS"}},"nopt":{"u":0},"desc":"detach device from ZFS mirror","u":[["NAME","<p><b>zpool-detach</b> — detach device from ZFS mirror</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<table> <tr> <td><b>zpool</b></td> <td><b>detach</b> <i>pool device</i></td> </tr> </table>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>Detaches <i>device</i> from a mirror. The operation is refused if there are no other valid replicas of the data. If <i>device</i> may be re-added to the pool later on then consider the <b>zpool</b> <b>offline</b> command instead.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p>zpool-attach(8), zpool-labelclear(8), zpool-offline(8), zpool-remove(8), zpool-replace(8), zpool-split(8)</p>"]]}